<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="protocol-twilight">Protocol Twilight</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a> is a new currency that players can earn from activating Protocol Twilight and killing bosses inside <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/dungeons/protocol-twilight-dungeons-overview">Elemental Rune Dungeons</a>. Each boss in a Protocol Inferno Dungeon will drop 2 Obsidian Fragments per player, with the final boss of each dungeon dropping an extra 3 Obsidian Fragments. With the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>, you can purchase every single item, including tier pieces, from the LFR system in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a> (which was ultimately scrapped for the Classic version of the game). <br/>
<br/>The order in which you pursue them will depend on your current gear but focus on acquiring the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-502/necrotic-boneplate-armor">tank tier</a> as it'll have great value as you step into raid.<br/>
<br/>Pieces like tier, weapons, and jewelry can be obtained from running the dungeons themselves as a drop from the last boss of the dungeon. So if you're planning to farm a lot of gear, use your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a> to buy gear not available from the dungeons.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="tier-bonuses-in-dragon-soul">Tier Bonuses in Dragon Soul</h3>As a <span class="c6">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif");'>Blood Death Knight</span></span>, our tier options in Phase 4 are of very high value. The <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-502/necrotic-boneplate-armor">tank tier</a> comes with the ability to turn our <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=55233/vampiric-blood">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_lifedrain.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vampiric Blood</span></a> into a raid-wide cooldown. <br/>
<br/>I cannot stress how good this tier bonus is during progression. The 4-set bonus takes 50% of the value from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=55233/vampiric-blood">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_lifedrain.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vampiric Blood</span></a> and applies it to your raid within a 100-yard radius. That means your raid will get an increased 12.5% healing taken and 7.5% of <b>your</b> maximum health. That's right, it doesn't give them a % health increase of their health in a way <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=97462/rallying-cry">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_toughness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rallying Cry</span></a>, but instead snapshots your current health values and gives 7.5% of that value to the raid, which ends up being more of an 11-13% health increase to the average raid member. <br/>
<br/>You can use <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=43554/glyph-of-vampiric-blood">
<img alt="Glyph of Vampiric Blood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glyph_majordeathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Vampiric Blood</span></a> to turn this into a 20% raid-wide healing received increase, but I generally wouldn't recommend using the glyph. <br/>
<br/>It is a bit unfortunate for us <span class="c6">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif");'>Blood Death Knight</span></span> that the tank 4-set is so strong for the raid, as from a personal gain perspective, we'd much rather play with the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item-set=-482/necrotic-boneplate-battlegear">DPS tier</a>. The set bonus is not that strong with the 2-set giving us 0 value and the 4-set giving us around 25% uptime of 710 Mastery, but the stats on these pieces are far better than the tank tier. <br/>
<br/>That being said, play with the tank 4-set in all circumstances during progression and after that point, you can start dabbling with the DPS 4-set and have some fun.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="gems-in-phase-4">Gems in Phase 4</h3>With the introduction of <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a>, we were also given the new <span class="q4">epic</span> version of gems, just like in TBC and WOTLK. In your pre-raid BIS journey, it is not expected of you to fully deck out your gear fully with epic gems. At least at the start of the phase they'll be very expensive. I've included <span class="q4">epic</span> gems in the lists below as they are indeed BIS, but unless you've had a lucky streak on your recent gold farming, stick to the <span class="q3">rare</span> version until you get a more permanent gear piece.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Blood Death Knight Tanking</h3>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="helm-for-blood-death-knight-tanking">Helm for Blood Death Knight Tanking</h4>
<span class="c6">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif");'>Blood Death Knight</span></span> will use 4-set bonuses in Phase 4, however, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78792/necrotic-boneplate-faceguard">
<img alt="Necrotic Boneplate Faceguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_plate_raiddeathknight_k_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Necrotic Boneplate Faceguard</span></a> is incredibly poorly statted for us and thus we prefer the Helmet to be our dedicated off-piece slot. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77155/visage-of-petrification">
<img alt="Visage of Petrification" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_plate_raiddeathknight_k_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Visage of Petrification</span></a> will be your best bet once you have the Valor to spare. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Helm Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62366/arcanum-of-the-earthen-ring">
<img alt="Arcanum of the Earthen Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of the Earthen Ring</span></a> which requires Revered with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1135/the-earthen-ring">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Earthen Ring</span></a> or <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62422/arcanum-of-the-wildhammer">
<img alt="Arcanum of the Wildhammer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of the Wildhammer</span></a> which requires Revered with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1174/wildhammer-clan">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Wildhammer Clan</span></a>/<wbr/>
<a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1172/dragonmaw-clan">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragonmaw Clan</span></a> for a more balanced/<wbr/>offensive approach.<br/>
<b>Recommended Meta Gem</b>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52294/austere-shadowspirit-diamond">
<img alt="Austere Shadowspirit Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_metagem_b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Austere Shadowspirit Diamond</span></a> will generally be your go-to meta gem, but <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68779/reverberating-shadowspirit-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Shadowspirit Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_metagem_b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Shadowspirit Diamond</span></a> will be a DPS upgrade of 300-500 DPS depending on your level of crit for a relatively small defensive loss.<div class="pad"></div>
